{"alias":"/schools/transportation/operation/drivers/eldt","title":"Entry-Level Driver Training (ELDT) – Coming 2/7/2022","changed":"2026-04-06T22:54:15+00:00","before":"<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.fmcsa.dot.gov%2Fnewsroom%2Fextension-compliance-date-entry-level-driver-training-0&amp;data=04%7C01%7CNathan.W.McIvor%40maine.gov%7C04cd0f729d504e0e52eb08d9851a067f%7C413fa8ab207d4b629bcdea1a8f2f864e%7C0%7C0%7C637687169082372802%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C1000&amp;sdata=SPUSgTc7f6bOtzZ7GbvUQbeAnkVWW1P%2FlomSG11ZtXk%3D&amp;reserved=0\">Extension of Compliance Date for Entry-Level Driver (ELDT) Training</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Federal Motor Carrier Safety Administration (FMCSA) extended the ELDT compliance date.&nbsp; FMCSA amended its December 8, 2016 final rule, \"Minimum Training Requirements for Entry-Level Commercial Motor Vehicle Operators\" (ELDT final rule), by extending the compliance date for the rule from February 7, 2020 to February 7, 2022.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>The FMCSA ELDT website is <a href=\"https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.fmcsa.dot.gov%2Fregistration%2Fcommercial-drivers-license%2Fentry-level-driver-training-eldt&amp;data=04%7C01%7CNathan.W.McIvor%40maine.gov%7C04cd0f729d504e0e52eb08d9851a067f%7C413fa8ab207d4b629bcdea1a8f2f864e%7C0%7C0%7C637687169082372802%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C1000&amp;sdata=mEnfmUlLYeVk2TyWZy5XeWy5M7AMAZSjFQoLP9AN7BI%3D&amp;reserved=0\">here</a>. The site provides an overview of Entry-Level Driver Training and the <a href=\"https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Ftpr.fmcsa.dot.gov%2F&amp;data=04%7C01%7CNathan.W.McIvor%40maine.gov%7C04cd0f729d504e0e52eb08d9851a067f%7C413fa8ab207d4b629bcdea1a8f2f864e%7C0%7C0%7C637687169082382765%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C1000&amp;sdata=2%2FLZshQ%2FwXooRva8YP7bxX0214%2FAgAuFDRDhhfG0O8A%3D&amp;reserved=0\">Training Provider Registry</a> and links information associated with ELDT.</li>\r\n\t<li>FMCSA ELDT frequently asked questions are <a href=\"https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.fmcsa.dot.gov%2Fregistration%2Fcommercial-drivers-license%2Feldt%2Ffaqs&amp;data=04%7C01%7CNathan.W.McIvor%40maine.gov%7C04cd0f729d504e0e52eb08d9851a067f%7C413fa8ab207d4b629bcdea1a8f2f864e%7C0%7C0%7C637687169082382765%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C1000&amp;sdata=iP%2BfqylcKM1HilmO0jHyzZXpv3zGVdr8%2F8DoyvEIln0%3D&amp;reserved=0\">here</a>.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.maine.gov%2Fsos%2Fbmv%2Fdriverridereducation%2FELDT.html&amp;data=04%7C01%7CNathan.W.McIvor%40maine.gov%7C04cd0f729d504e0e52eb08d9851a067f%7C413fa8ab207d4b629bcdea1a8f2f864e%7C0%7C0%7C637687169082382765%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C1000&amp;sdata=sdo%2FEegsBfy6m62lixNZ3s9vseLWO1%2FRVtunJeNHav0%3D&amp;reserved=0\">Maine Bureau of Motor Vehicles Entry-Level Driver Training</a> (ELDT)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This Maine Bureau of Motor Vehicles website explains the baseline for training requirements for entry-level drivers, who the ELDT does not apply to and what the FMCSA <a href=\"https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Ftpr.fmcsa.dot.gov%2F&amp;data=04%7C01%7CNathan.W.McIvor%40maine.gov%7C04cd0f729d504e0e52eb08d9851a067f%7C413fa8ab207d4b629bcdea1a8f2f864e%7C0%7C0%7C637687169082392717%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C1000&amp;sdata=e3byT%2Bu18E6PowqyG0H09iLZAwJfU%2BnEGsjvpwpx7Io%3D&amp;reserved=0\">Training Provider Registry</a> will retain. The site also includes information about exceptions for taking a skills test and FMCSA information sheets.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n","after":"<div class=\"doe-hero\">\n<p class=\"doe-eyebrow\">School Bus Drivers</p>\n<p class=\"doe-lead\">Federal Motor Carrier Safety Administration (FMCSA) extended the ELDT compliance date. FMCSA amended its December 8, 2016 final rule, \"Minimum Training Requirements for Entry-Level Commercial Motor Vehicle Operators\" (ELDT final rule), by extending the compliance date for the rule from February 7, 2020 to February 7, 2022.</p>\n<p class=\"doe-cta\"><a class=\"btn-cta\" href=\"https://www.fmcsa.dot.gov/newsroom/extension-compliance-date-entry-level-driver-training-0\">Extension of Compliance Date for Entry-Level Driver (ELDT) Training</a></p>\n\n</div>\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>The FMCSA ELDT website is <a href=\"https://www.fmcsa.dot.gov/registration/commercial-drivers-license/entry-level-driver-training-eldt\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. The site provides an overview of Entry-Level Driver Training and the <a href=\"https://tpr.fmcsa.dot.gov/\" target=\"_blank\">Training Provider Registry</a> and links information associated with ELDT.</li>\r\n\t<li>FMCSA ELDT frequently asked questions are <a href=\"https://www.fmcsa.dot.gov/registration/commercial-drivers-license/eldt/faqs\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"doe-action\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/sos/bmv/driverridereducation/ELDT.html\">Maine Bureau of Motor Vehicles Entry-Level Driver Training</a> (ELDT)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This Maine Bureau of Motor Vehicles website explains the baseline for training requirements for entry-level drivers, who the ELDT does not apply to and what the FMCSA <a href=\"https://tpr.fmcsa.dot.gov/\" target=\"_blank\">Training Provider Registry</a> will retain. The site also includes information about exceptions for taking a skills test and FMCSA information sheets.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\n<p class=\"doe-top\"><a href=\"#top\">Back to top</a></p>","notes":[],"decisions":[{"id":"deck","on":true,"label":"Use this paragraph as the page description","why":"It is the page’s own opening paragraph, moved into the banner rather than rewritten.","value":"Federal Motor Carrier Safety Administration (FMCSA) extended the ELDT compliance date. FMCSA amended its December 8, 2016 final rule, \"Minimum Training Requirements for Entry-Level Commercial Motor Vehicle Operators\" (ELDT final rule), by extending the compliance date for the rule from February 7, 2020 to February 7, 2022."},{"id":"leadbtn","on":true,"label":"Put the page’s one action in the banner","why":"This page opens with a paragraph holding nothing but \"Extension of Compliance Date for Entry-Level Driver (ELDT) Training\" — the first thing it asks you to do, set as a line of body text. The banner has a place for exactly that, so it moves there as a button. The link and its words are unchanged; only where it sits changes.","value":"Extension of Compliance Date for Entry-Level Driver (ELDT) Training"},{"id":"eyebrow","on":true,"label":"Eyebrow: \"School Bus Drivers\"","why":"Taken from the parent page, /schools/transportation/operation/drivers."}],"mechanical":["safelinks unwrapped: 6","empty paragraphs removed: 2","target set by destination: 5","action links marked: 2"],"findings":[{"name":"link-text-that-says-nothing","n":2,"eg":["here","here"]}],"safe":true,"audit":{"alias":"/schools/transportation/operation/drivers/eldt","title":"Entry-Level Driver Training (ELDT) – Coming 2/7/2022","changed":"2026-04-06T22:54:15+00:00","words":148,"bytes":3900,"fixes":["safelinks unwrapped: 6","empty paragraphs removed: 2","target set by destination: 5","action links marked: 2"],"flags":["no section-header device"],"contentSafe":true,"headings":[],"outline":[],"components":{"cards":0,"cardHeaders":0,"cardTitles":0,"accordions":0,"tables":0,"dataTables":0,"contactCube":0,"jumbotron":0,"dcNote":0,"blockheads":0,"videos":0,"images":0,"buttons":0},"access":{"ima